<item><title>Staff at AGL Guinée and Conakry Terminal offered cancer screening through 9 December</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/gn/staff-at-agl-guinee-and-conakry-terminal-offered-cancer-cf3d6b/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/gn/staff-at-agl-guinee-and-conakry-terminal-offered-cancer-cf3d6b/</guid><category>Guinea</category><description>More than 500 employees joined prevention sessions from 16 to 18 November, with urologists answering questions anonymously.</description><pubDate>Thu, 26 Nov 2026 09:03:00 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/gn.jpg" length="31286" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/gn.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
<item><title>Guinea learns U15 school football opponents and qualification routes</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/gn/guinea-learns-u15-school-football-opponents-and-7ab2ea/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/gn/guinea-learns-u15-school-football-opponents-and-7ab2ea/</guid><category>Guinea</category><description>The boys face four teams, while the girls must finish first in a three-team group to reach the African finals.</description><pubDate>Thu, 26 Nov 2026 06:44:51 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/gn.jpg" length="31286" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/gn.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
<item><title>Diaka Camara Foundation trains students at three Conakry schools on abuse</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/gn/diaka-camara-foundation-trains-students-at-three-conakry-63b278/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/gn/diaka-camara-foundation-trains-students-at-three-conakry-63b278/</guid><category>Guinea</category><description>The sessions cover physical, psychological and sexual violence, harassment and early marriage, with Guinea’s child-protection office supplying trainers.</description><pubDate>Wed, 25 Nov 2026 22:30:17 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/gn.jpg" length="31286" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/gn.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
<item><title>Guinea approves sovereign fund with 30% of Simandou revenues</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/gn/guinea-approves-sovereign-fund-with-30-of-simandou-revenues-d85f10/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/gn/guinea-approves-sovereign-fund-with-30-of-simandou-revenues-d85f10/</guid><category>Guinea</category><description>The law directs 30% of the project’s tax and non-tax receipts to the fund and sets out contributions totalling 900 million dollars over five years.</description><pubDate>Wed, 25 Nov 2026 19:30:41 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/gn/guinea-approves-sovereign-fund-with-30-of-simandou-revenues-d85f10/share.jpg" length="42500" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/gn/guinea-approves-sovereign-fund-with-30-of-simandou-revenues-d85f10/share.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
<item><title>Guinea offers investors a $1.9 billion port and rail-zone projects in Morocco</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/gn/guinea-offers-investors-a-1-9-billion-port-and-rail-zone-521ced/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/gn/guinea-offers-investors-a-1-9-billion-port-and-rail-zone-521ced/</guid><category>Guinea</category><description>The government says the country drew $7.8 billion in foreign direct investment in 2025, the largest sum in West Africa.</description><pubDate>Wed, 25 Nov 2026 18:56:01 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/gn.jpg" length="31286" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/gn.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
